# Sub-agent isolated worktrees (Agent tool with `isolation: worktree`).
# Each agent gets its own .claude/worktrees/agent-<id>/ checkout that is
# auto-cleaned at the end of the agent run; we don't want git to track them
# while they exist.
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-session kaizen scratch file. Maintained during a task, consumed by
# /after-task-dantotsus once the work merges. Local-only by design.
KAIZEN.md

# Working file for the current refactoring branch (see the PR description).
REFACTORING-BRIEF.md
.eslintcache
.eslintcache
node_modules/.cache
.stryker-tmp
reports

# Every architecture page, of both kinds, for the same reason: it is generated,
# and whoever reads it builds it first.
#
# `<app>-diff.html` describes a branch rather than the repository, so there is
# no revision it would be true at. `<app>-architecture.html` and `index.html`
# describe the repository, but `pages.yml` regenerates before publishing and
# `architecture.yml` regenerates before diffing a pull request, so no consumer
# ever opened the committed bytes — they cost 9.3 MB rewritten in full on every
# change, and bought a byte gate whose only subject was its own output.
#
# The model beside each page is committed: it is small, it diffs as prose, and
# every byte of it comes from the working tree, so a gate on it means something.
docs/architecture/*.html
